# Agent/skill definition files are distributed verbatim to other repos and
# parsed by both pwsh and POSIX-shell tooling (tools/ai-bootstrap, tools/workflow).
# Pin LF so a Windows checkout never reintroduces CRLF that breaks Linux-run
# scripts or produces noisy whole-file diffs.
claude-agents/*.md text eol=lf
agents/*.agent.md text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, sharper consequence: tools/workflow/isolation/git-wrapper.sh
# is bind-mounted into a Linux container (workflow/isolation.md section 3 --
# containers are always Linux, never Windows containers) and run via its
# #!/bin/sh shebang. A CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true is a common Windows
# Git default, even though this dev machine happens to have it off) turns
# that into `#!/bin/sh\r`, which the kernel's script loader can't resolve --
# a hard exec failure inside the container, not just dirty diffs. Pinning
# every *.sh in the repo, not just this one file, since the same risk class
# applies to anything here a Linux-targeted shell eventually runs.
*.sh text eol=lf
